 "description": "The Maryland Energy Assistance Program (MEAP) provides free utility repairs or replacements for income-eligible households.",
 "main_html": "<main id=\"main-content\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<div>\n<div id=\"block-maryland-hero\">\n<section aria-labelledby=\"node-62-title\" class=\"maryland-hero maryland-hero--basic has-illustration no-image\">\n<div class=\"maryland-hero__container\">\n<div class=\"maryland-hero__content\">\n<div class=\"maryland-hero__breadcrumb\">\n<div class=\"maryland-breadcrumb__wrapper maryland-breadcrumb__wrapper--dark\">\n<nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumbs\" class=\"usa-breadcrumb maryland-breadcrumb maryland-breadcrumb--dark\">\n<ol class=\"usa-breadcrumb__list maryland-breadcrumb__list\">\n<li class=\"usa-breadcrumb__list-item maryland-breadcrumb__list-item\">\n<a class=\"usa-breadcrumb__link maryland-breadcrumb__link\" href=\"/\">\n<span>Home</span>\n</a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"usa-breadcrumb__list-item maryland-breadcrumb__list-item\">\n<a class=\"usa-breadcrumb__link maryland-breadcrumb__link\" href=\"/energy-home-repair\">\n<span>Energy &amp; Home Repair</span>\n</a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"usa-breadcrumb__list-item maryland-breadcrumb__list-item\">\n<a class=\"usa-breadcrumb__link maryland-breadcrumb__link\" href=\"/energy-home-repair/energy-grants-and-loans-residents\">\n<span>Energy Grants and Loans for Residents</span>\n</a>\n</li>\n<li aria-current=\"page\" class=\"usa-breadcrumb__list-item maryland-breadcrumb__list-item usa-current\">\n<span class=\"usa-breadcrumb__link maryland-breadcrumb__link\">\n<span>Maryland Energy Assistance Program</span>\n</span>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</nav>\n</div>\n</div>\n<h1 class=\"maryland-hero__title\" id=\"node-62-title\"><span>Maryland Energy Assistance Program (MEAP)</span>\n</h1>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n<div class=\"hidden\" data-drupal-messages-fallback=\"\"></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"grid-container\">\n<div class=\"maryland-page-alerts margin-top-6\">\n<div>\n<div class=\"views-element-container\" id=\"block-maryland-views-block-local-alerts-site-wide\">\n<div><div class=\"js-view-dom-id-b11efaeefafd08f9156ca9f12db33bc426fab9bbdbe9cebeff17f24feaaad454\">\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"views-element-container\" id=\"block-maryland-views-block-local-alerts-page-specific\">\n<div><div class=\"js-view-dom-id-804d87c285354628c4f3563643066687fc6659b0da7b61daf6aca494f7617f5c\">\n<div><div aria-labelledby=\"alert\" class=\"maryland-alert maryland-alert--info desktop:margin-top-3\" role=\"status\">\n<div class=\"maryland-alert__container\">\n<div class=\"maryland-alert__body\">\n<h2 class=\"maryland-alert__heading\" id=\"alert\">Attention: The Limited Flood Assistance Program closed on May 31, 2026</h2>\n<div class=\"maryland-alert__text\">\n<p>The program provided special flood assistance to eligible homes in Allegany and Garrett counties. For more program details, view Maryland Energy Assistance Program (MEAP)-Flood Assistance​ announcement.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"grid-container\">\n<div class=\"grid-row grid-gap\">\n<aside class=\"layout-sidebar-first grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-3 margin-top-8 desktop:margin-top-10 desktop:margin-bottom-15\" role=\"complementary\">\n<a class=\"usa-skipnav maryland-link maryland-link--skipnav\" href=\"#page-content\">Skip sidebar navigation</a>\n<nav aria-labelledby=\"sidenav-title\" class=\"maryland-sidenav\">\n<button aria-controls=\"sidenav\" class=\"maryland-sidenav__toggle\" type=\"button\">\n<span class=\"usa-sr-only\">Close</span>\n<h2 class=\"maryland-sidenav__title\" id=\"sidenav-title\">Section Menu</h2>\n</button>\n<ul class=\"maryland-sidenav__list maryland-sidenav__list--level-1\" data-region=\"sidebar_first\" id=\"sidenav\">\n<li class=\"maryland-sidenav__item maryland-sidenav__item--level-1\">\n<a class=\"maryland-sidenav__link maryland-sidenav__link--level-1\" data-drupal-link-system-path=\"node/760\" href=\"/energy-home-repair/energy-grants-and-loans-residents\">Energy Grants and Loans for Residents</a>\n<ul class=\"maryland-sidenav__list maryland-sidenav__list--level-2\" data-region=\"sidebar_first\">\n<li class=\"maryland-sidenav__item maryland-sidenav__item--level-2\">\n<a class=\"maryland-sidenav__link maryland-sidenav__link--level-2\" data-drupal-link-system-path=\"node/60\" href=\"/energy-home-repair/energy-grants-and-loans-residents/empower\">EmPOWER</a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"maryland-sidenav__item maryland-sidenav__item--level-2\">\n<span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"maryland-sidenav__link maryland-sidenav__link--level-2\">Maryland Energy Assistance Program</span>\n</li>\n<li class=\"maryland-sidenav__item maryland-sidenav__item--level-2\">\n<a class=\"maryland-sidenav__link maryland-sidenav__link--level-2\" data-drupal-link-system-path=\"node/61\" href=\"/energy-home-repair/energy-grants-and-loans-residents/weatherization-assistance-program-wap\">Weatherization Assistance Program (WAP)</a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"maryland-sidenav__item maryland-sidenav__item--level-2\">\n<a class=\"maryland-sidenav__link maryland-sidenav__link--level-2\" data-drupal-link-system-path=\"node/63\" href=\"/energy-home-repair/energy-grants-and-loans-residents/besmart-home-loan-program\">BeSMART Home Loan Program</a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"maryland-sidenav__item maryland-sidenav__item--level-2\">\n<a class=\"maryland-sidenav__link maryland-sidenav__link--level-2\" data-drupal-link-system-path=\"node/64\" href=\"/energy-home-repair/energy-grants-and-loans-residents/net-zero-loan-program\">Net Zero Loan Program</a>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</nav>\n</aside>\n<div class=\"margin-y-8 desktop:margin-top-10 desktop:margin-bottom-15 grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-8\" id=\"page-content\">\n<div>\n<div aria-labelledby=\"summary-box\" class=\"maryland-summary-box\" role=\"region\">\n<div class=\"maryland-summary-box__inner\">\n<h2 class=\"maryland-summary-box__heading\" id=\"summary-box\">\n          Funding update\n        </h2>\n<div class=\"maryland-summary-box__text\">\n<ul class=\"maryland-summary-box__list\">\n<li><p><strong>Funding status:</strong> Funding is fully spent for 2025–2026 (Waitlist only — assistance is not guaranteed)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Next funding cycle: </strong> November 1, 2026 (October 1 for Garrett County only) - September 30, 2027, depending on available funding.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Other fundings:</strong> For heating, cooling, or hot water repairs, you may qualify for grants or low-interest loans through our <a class=\"maryland-link\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"8737b194-2d68-40e9-81aa-3c19c725babb\" href=\"/energy-home-repair/homeowner-repair-loans-grants\" title=\"Homeowner Repair Loans &amp; Grants\">home repair programs</a>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>For utility bill assistance:</strong> Call 800-332-6347 or contact your local county's Energy Assistance office (OHEP)​.<strong> </strong>We do not provide bill pay assistance.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"usa-prose maryland-toc-target\">\n<div class=\"maryland-toc\">\n</div>\n<p>MEAP helps eligible Maryland households repair or replace heating, cooling, and water heating systems at no cost. The program operates year-round and is federally funded to make homes more comfortable.</p><h2>MEAP priority schedule</h2><p>During priority seasons, qualified clients with non-functioning heating or cooling systems receive priority. </p><ul><li><strong>No cool program</strong><ul><li>Priority season: March 1 – June 30</li></ul></li><li><strong>No heat program</strong><ul><li>Priority season: July 1 – September 30</li><li>Heating services continue: November 1 – March 1</li></ul></li><li><strong>Hot water heater program</strong><ul><li>Hot water heater services have priority only when there is no waitlist for heating or cooling assistance</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Current status: </strong>There is a waitlist for all services.</p><h2><strong>​</strong>Eligibility</h2><p>To be eligible for the MEAP program, you must:​</p><ol><li>Meet income qualifications.<strong> </strong>Your household income needs to be lower than the limits based on household size, as shown in the Income Limits table.</li><li>Have a non-functioning heating, cooling, and/or water heating system.</li></ol><p>What kind of work will be eligible is based on a home assessment and funding availability.</p><h3>Maximum annual household income</h3><div class=\"maryland-table-container--scrollable\" tabindex=\"0\"><table class=\"maryland-table\"><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\"><strong>​​Household Size​</strong></th><th scope=\"col\"><strong>​​​​​​Annual Gross Income Based on 200% Federal Poverty Level</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>​1</td><td>$31,920</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>$43,280</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>$54,640</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>$66,000</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>$77,360</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>$88,720</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>$100,080</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>$111,440</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>$122,800</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>$134,160</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>$145,520</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>$156,880</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>$168,240</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>$179,600</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>​Note:</strong> Add $11,360 for each additional household member over 14.<br/><strong>Updated:</strong>​ 2/10/2026</p><h3>​​​​​​​Accepted as income-eligible​</h3><p>If you are currently an eligible participant in one of these programs, you are automatically income-eligible for weatherization services:</p><ul><li>Utility Bill Pay Assistance through OHEP</li><li>Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP)</li><li>Temporary Assistance for Needy Families (TANF)</li><li>Supplemental Security Income (SSI)</li><li>HUD housing assistance programs</li></ul><p>Program​s <strong>NOT accepted</strong> as income-eligible:</p><ul><li>Fuel Fund Assistance</li><li>DHCD Rehab Programs</li><li>Baltimore Lead Hazard Control Program</li><li>Medicaid</li><li>MEA Energy Equity Grant</li><li>MEEHA</li><li>Geographical eligibility for certain areas</li></ul><h2>How the pro​gram works</h2><ol><li><strong>Home assessment:</strong> Once you are approved, a local agency will contact you to schedule an in-home assessment. This evaluation determines your home's specific service needs and identifies ways to increase the comfort of your home.</li><li><strong>Review assessment: </strong>The local agency will review the assessment results with you.</li><li><strong>Contractor scheduling: </strong>The local agency will schedule an approved contractor to come to your home and complete the recommended work.</li></ol><h2>How to apply</h2><p><strong>Important funding notice: </strong>Funding for the 2025–2026 has been fully expended. You may submit an application to join the waitlist, but we cannot guarantee assistance for clients who are placed on the waitlist during this funding cycle.</p><p>Complete a program application and submit all required documents to our office by mail. </p><ul><li><a class=\"maryland-link\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"media\" data-entity-uuid=\"73c709de-7c6d-4b38-9ad8-3e4694096d5e\" href=\"/media/587\" title=\"Whole Home Application\">Download the program ​application​ form - PDF - 272.69 KB</a></li></ul><p>If you are <strong>currently approved to receive Energy Assistance payments</strong> from the Maryland Department of Human Services, you may contact our intake line at <a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"tel:+8555838976\">1-855-583-8976</a>​.</p><h2>Resources for renters</h2><p>Due to limited funding and a homeowner waitlist, MEAP prioritizes homeowners for heating, cooling, and hot water repair or replacement services. </p><p>For information on tenant rights, landlord responsibilities, and other available resources, please visit the <a class=\"maryland-link\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"57239fed-bde3-4cc3-bbbc-e0ba96a9ad09\" href=\"/housing/renter-landlord-resources/tenant-and-landlord-affairs\" title=\"Tenant and Landlord Affairs\">Tenant and Landlord Affairs</a>​.</p><h2>Contact information</h2><p>Program: Housing and Building Energy Programs<br/>Toll-Free (Maryland Only): <a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"tel:+8555838976\">1-855-583-8976</a></p>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"automatic-list-995\" class=\"maryland-automatic-list\">\n<div class=\"maryland-card-group__header\">\n<div class=\"maryland-card-group__header-content\">\n<h2 class=\"maryland-card-group__title\" id=\"automatic-list-995\"><span>Latest energy news</span>\n</h2>\n</div>\n<div class=\"maryland-card-group__more-link\">\n<a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"/news-stories\">\n          See all news\n        </a>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div><div class=\"views-element-container\" id=\"block-views-block-automatic-list-blocks-content-block-automatic-list-news\">\n<div><div class=\"js-view-dom-id-4d3cc31387fb3ad28b419cfde3efe2c649c8d25b657e4f62ffc076d7993b3427\">\n<ul class=\"maryland-card-group\">\n<li class=\"maryland-card maryland-card--linked\" id=\"auto-list-item\">\n<a aria-label=\"&lt;span&gt;Public Hearing for Weatherization State Plan - Sep 15, 2026&lt;/span&gt;\n\" class=\"maryland-card__link\" href=\"/news-stories/public-notices/public-hearing-weatherization-state-plan-sep-15-2026\">\n<div class=\"maryland-card__container\">\n<div class=\"maryland-card__media\">\n<div class=\"maryland-card__img\">\n<picture>\n<source height=\"450\" media=\"all and (min-width: 500px)\" sizes=\"100vw\" srcset=\"https://cdn.maryland.gov/maryland-cms/prod/dhcd/s3fs-public/styles/4_3_500x375_focal_point_webp/public/images/2026-06/dhcd-public-notice-2026.jpg.webp?versionId=vcLBvg38IU7fjoUxBiApolhLrok.HzkB&amp;X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&amp;X-Amz-Security-Token=IQoJb3JpZ2luX2VjEHgaCXVzLWVhc3QtMSJHMEUCIAs91ibUre4l9P%2BdU0Cprz/avdy1ucDILV4vAq7fxbAWAiEA4sDKzxhVeRtKVzQ5qAJYqNtoCHYnqCdtdt14vdJJpAoqugUIQBAAGgw3MTYwNjc2Njc5NDIiDJwO85CTgt/RPQSXEiqXBWYbWymiBJgqp4D8Hnz4XnCPh%2BRICtXzpe00RL0aRdjj3A